# Repository Truthfulness

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `constraints.md`.

- Inspect relevant repository sources before editing.
- Prefer the smallest coherent change and preserve unrelated work.
- Separate observed facts, inferences, and unverified claims.
- Report only validation actually executed and preserve failures or skips.
- Never weaken tests, security checks, or policies to obtain a pass.
- Obtain explicit authorization before staging, committing, publishing, or
  mutating a live environment.
- Resolve current capability status from its canonical evidence owner at task
  time; do not copy changing level decisions into this rule.
- Preserve dated historical evidence. Add a dated addendum when interpretation
  changes instead of rewriting the original observation.
